      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s still quite a bit of tricky logic left here, I wonder if it would clean up better if we used an abstraction to encapsulate the switcheroo:\n\n```\n    // Offers writable path semantics by wrapping either a non-const path (which can be modified\n    // directly) or a const path (in which case we use a scratch buffer).\n    class AutoMutablePath {\n    public:\n        explicit AutoMutablePath(const SkPath\u0026 p) : fImmutablePath(\u0026p) {}\n        explicit AutoMutablePath(SkPath\u0026 p) : fMutablePath(\u0026p) { fMutablePath-\u003esetIsVolatile(true); }\n\n        operator const SkPath\u0026() const {\n            if (fMutablePath) {\n                SkASSERT(!fScratch.isValid());\n                return *fMutablePath;\n            }\n\n            SkASSERT(fImmutablePath);\n            return fScratch.isValid() ? *fScratch : *fImmutablePath;\n        }\n        const SkPath* operator-\u003e() const { return \u0026(this-\u003eoperator const SkPath\u0026()); }\n\n        SkPath* writable() {\n            if (fMutablePath) {\n                return fMutablePath;\n            }\n\n            if (!fScratch.isValid()) {\n                fScratch.init();\n                fScratch-\u003esetIsVolatile(true);\n            }\n\n            return fScratch.get();\n        }\n\n    private:\n        const SkPath*   fImmutablePath \u003d nullptr;\n        SkPath*         fMutablePath   \u003d nullptr;\n        SkTLazy\u003cSkPath\u003e fScratch;\n    };\n```\n\nThen if we pass in an `AutoMutablePath path` we should be able to write stuff like\n\n`path-\u003etransform(..., path.writable())`, `drawDevPath(path, ...)`, etc.",
      "revId": "cebb47300b64145d07c9b8fb74709722991d22d1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
